        "title": "Candidate minus its declared control"
      },
      {
        "body": "Pullback uses a completed return bar after one opposing bar and measures one future bar against all unfiltered snapbacks. Exhaustion compares a wait-for-second-reversal policy with the early policy on every original opportunity, using three future bars. Quiet breakout uses a low prior thirty-minute bar count and a two-bar extreme break, against the same breakout without low activity. Entry and exit are next-bar open references; wait opportunities without confirmation contribute zero and incur no assumed cost. Net deducts two ticks per executed round trip. The contrast interval is the saved 99.44% session-cluster familywise interval for nine comparisons.",
        "id": "methods",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Definitions and methods"
      },
      {
        "body": "All dates were retrospectively inspected. Completion is only a next-bar-start proxy; timezone, intrabar order, bid/ask and fills are unverified. The run used older export-clock inputs; later clock correction does not change this sealed cohort or its quiet-period calibration. Assumed tick haircuts do not establish executable net profitability.",
        "id": "limitations",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Limitations and uncertainty"
